Project Design – Phase Details
Phase 1: Requirement Analysis
Objective: Identify the needs of students and define what EduGenie should provide.
Activities:
•	Identify the target users (students, teachers, and learners).
•	Analyze common learning difficulties.
•	Define the required AI-based learning features.
•	Identify functional and non-functional requirements.
•	Select Google Gemini as the AI model for generating learning assistance.
Expected Output:
•	Requirement specification document.
•	List of system features.
•	User roles and use cases.
________________________________________
Phase 2: System Design
Objective: Design the overall architecture and workflow of EduGenie.
Major Components:
•	User Interface: Provides chat and learning interfaces.
•	Application Backend: Handles requests, authentication, and application logic.
•	Gemini API: Processes user questions and generates AI-based responses.
•	Database: Stores user profiles, learning history, questions, and preferences.
•	Learning Module: Organizes explanations, summaries, quizzes, and study materials.
Basic Architecture:
        Student
           |
           v
    EduGenie Interface
           |
           v
     Application Server
       /           \
      v             v
  Database      Gemini API
                    |
                    v
             AI-Generated Response
                    |
                    v
              Student Interface
Expected Output:
•	System architecture diagram.
•	Database design.
•	UI design/wireframes.
•	Module specifications.
________________________________________
Phase 3: AI Integration
Objective: Integrate Google Gemini into EduGenie to provide personalized learning assistance.
Activities:
•	Configure Gemini API access.
•	Design prompts for educational queries.
•	Send student questions to Gemini.
•	Process and display Gemini responses.
•	Implement context-aware conversations.
•	Add safeguards for inappropriate or unreliable responses.
Example:
Student:
"Explain photosynthesis in simple terms."

        ↓

EduGenie

        ↓

Gemini API

        ↓

"Photosynthesis is the process by which
plants use sunlight, water and carbon
dioxide to produce food and oxygen."

        ↓

Student
Expected Output:
•	Functional Gemini integration.
•	AI-powered question-answering module.
________________________________________
Phase 4: Learning Feature Development
Objective: Develop the major educational features of EduGenie.
Possible Features:
•	AI Chat Assistant – Answers academic questions.
•	Topic Explanation – Explains difficult concepts in simple language.
•	Summarization – Converts lengthy content into concise notes.
•	Quiz Generation – Creates questions from a selected topic.
•	Question Generation – Generates practice questions.
•	Study Planner – Helps organize learning activities.
•	Personalized Learning – Adjusts explanations according to the learner's requirements.
•	Revision Assistant – Provides quick revision material.
•	Doubt Clearing – Allows students to ask follow-up questions.
Expected Output:
•	Completed learning modules.
•	Integrated AI learning workflow.
________________________________________
Phase 5: Database Development
Objective: Store and manage relevant student and learning information.
Possible Tables/Collections:
Table	Purpose
Users	Stores student account information
Subjects	Stores subject details
Topics	Stores learning topics
Questions	Stores questions and interactions
Quiz	Stores generated quizzes
Results	Stores quiz performance
LearningHistory	Stores previous learning activities
Expected Output:
•	Functional database.
•	Proper relationships between entities.
•	Secure data-management mechanism.
________________________________________
Phase 6: User Interface Development
Objective: Create a simple and user-friendly learning environment.
Main Screens:
1.	Login/Registration
2.	Student Dashboard
3.	AI Chat Interface
4.	Subject Selection
5.	Topic Explanation
6.	Quiz Interface
7.	Quiz Results
8.	Learning History
9.	Study Planner
10.	Profile/Settings
Design Principles:
•	Simple navigation.
•	Mobile-friendly interface.
•	Clear typography.
•	Easy-to-understand AI responses.
•	Minimal distractions.
________________________________________
Phase 7: Testing
Objective: Verify that EduGenie works correctly and produces useful responses.
Types of Testing:
•	Unit Testing: Test individual modules.
•	Integration Testing: Test interaction between the application, database, and Gemini API.
•	Functional Testing: Verify that each feature works as intended.
•	UI Testing: Check usability and responsiveness.
•	Performance Testing: Measure response time and system performance.
•	Security Testing: Test authentication and protection of user information.
•	AI Response Testing: Evaluate responses for relevance, clarity, and factual reliability.
Expected Output:
•	Test cases.
•	Test results.
•	Bug reports and fixes.
________________________________________
Phase 8: Evaluation
Objective: Determine whether EduGenie meets its educational objectives.
Evaluation Parameters:
•	Accuracy of AI-generated responses.
•	Response time.
•	Ease of use.
•	Student satisfaction.
•	Quiz performance.
•	Relevance of generated learning content.
•	Personalization effectiveness.
Possible Evaluation Method:
Students use EduGenie
        ↓
Complete learning activities
        ↓
Take quizzes
        ↓
Provide feedback
        ↓
Analyze performance
        ↓
Improve the system
________________________________________
Phase 9: Deployment
Objective: Make the completed EduGenie system available to users.
Activities:
•	Configure production environment.
•	Deploy frontend and backend.
•	Configure Gemini API securely.
•	Configure database.
•	Perform final system testing.
•	Monitor application performance.
Expected Output:
•	Fully deployed EduGenie application.
